<!-- MUSCLE GLYPH - SHOULDERS. The head over the deltoid yoke: the top of the body, cut
     off at the armpits.

     ONE PART, drawn alone, in the equipment set's lane: stroke only, 1.8 wide, round
     caps and joins, nothing filled (owner, 2026-10-11: *"clean muscle group icons of
     body parts, arm leg etc etc ... remake them to actually match with the icons you
     drew for the equipments"*).

     WHERE THE LINES GO, and why there are only two. The yoke on its own was a bell, so
     each deltoid gets one short arc down its inside - the same move the rack makes with
     its two pegs, a line that says what the outline cannot. There is no chest on it, no
     spine, no arms: those belong to the glyphs next door, and the filter row draws all
     six at once.

     WIDE AND FLAT on purpose - see the note in [ic_muscle_chest]: at 22dp the shoulder
     yoke is told from the chest's tall bust by silhouette alone. It is also centred in
     its box rather than hung from the top - [MuscleGlyphFamilyTest] rasterises each
     glyph and requires its ink to clear all four edges, which is what caught this one
     sitting high in its box. -->
